WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:03.503
A liberal arts education basically
just means that you have the opportunity

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:04.212
to explore

00:00:04.212 --> 00:00:07.841
a bunch of different disciplines
and kind of find what fits you the best.

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:11.720
My own world arts
experience has allowed me to explore

00:00:11.761 --> 00:00:14.264
topics that I like
that are really different.

00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:17.350
I've taken cellular biology classes,
I've taken

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.478
Japanese language classes,
I've taken history classes.

00:00:20.478 --> 00:00:20.895
Two weeks

00:00:20.895 --> 00:00:24.315
after I got here, decided I want to do
molecular biology and biochemistry.

00:00:24.733 --> 00:00:26.484
A month later decided that wasn't me.

00:00:26.484 --> 00:00:29.446
And then at the end of my sophomore year,
ended up taking a psychology

00:00:29.446 --> 00:00:31.823
class, discovering
I really like psychology.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:35.201
I decided to do psychology
with a concentration in neuroscience.

00:00:35.577 --> 00:00:38.955
The opportunity
to take things alongside art

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:42.625
has really fulfilled my need to explore.

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:46.254
I was able to take
so many different classes my first year

00:00:46.254 --> 00:00:49.507
alone, and through that was able
to discover what I want to do.

00:00:49.924 --> 00:00:53.470
That's really the whole approach
to education here at Yale,

00:00:53.678 --> 00:00:56.556
is that, you know,
you have the freedom to explore

00:00:56.806 --> 00:01:01.227
all different majors and opportunities
and academic programs that we offer

00:01:01.352 --> 00:01:03.313
to figure out
what the best fit for you is.

